fmt uses malloc and free and includes neither.

format.h opens by defining _LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES -- it asks the
standard library not to hand it anything it did not ask for -- and then calls
malloc and free in fmt::detail::allocator without including <cstdlib>. Every
other header it includes happens to declare them on a desktop, so this holds
everywhere it has been built.

Against bionic's headers it does not, and the compiler says what it found
instead:

    error: use of undeclared identifier 'malloc'; did you mean 'tzalloc'?
    error: 'tzalloc' is unavailable: introduced in Android 35

The include is added where the others are, spelled the same way.

--- a/fmt-11.1.1/include/fmt/format.h
+++ b/fmt-11.1.1/include/fmt/format.h
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #  include <cmath>    // std::signbit
 #  include <cstddef>  // std::byte
 #  include <cstdint>  // uint32_t
+#  include <cstdlib>  // std::malloc, std::free
 #  include <cstring>  // std::memcpy
 #  include <limits>   // std::numeric_limits
 #  include <new>      // std::bad_alloc
